  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-05-28T00:36:41.567Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, the fallback shader system requires editing the shader itself to control selected fallback shader. This is inconvenient for two reasons.\nFirst, shader editing is beyond the knowledge of many people doing basic avatar editing. It requires leaving the unity editor and making changes to text files. Moving this into the editor itself would make the shader fallback much more accessible.\nThe second issue is the situation where you want the same shader to have multiple fallback behaviors. For example, wanting a shader that can optionally include transparency to generally fall back to the standard toon shader, but in situations where a transparent effect would look terrible without tranperency such as a facial expression overlay wanting it to fall back to simply hidden. This currently requires making a second copy of the shader with the only change being the fallback tags.\nMoving this out of text files and the shader layer and into the editor and the material layer would resolve both of these issues.",
